//
// The prefill of a pass's rows through two layers, a command each
// (aie2_prefill_layer.py) on NPU2, at block 1 of a 256-row KV cache, each
// row's embed seed made on the device: the residual leaving the last layer
// and block 1's KV rows in both layers bit-exact to llama_oracle.Layer.forward,
// every row. --synthetic-weights uses seeded random layers and embed table.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, xrt_python_bindings, xrt_python_ctrl_scratchpad_bo
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_prefill_layer.py --synthetic-weights --block 1 --layers 2 --t 256 | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: residual leaving layer 1: 64/64 rows bit-exact
// CHECK: block 1's KV rows, all layers: 64/64 rows bit-exact
// CHECK: prefill of 2 layers, block 1, 64 rows: PASS
//
// A pass of 36 rows: two embed commands (28 and 8 rows), three of the
// attention's four sub-batches, and block 1's last 28 rows left as they were.
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_prefill_layer.py --synthetic-weights --block 1 --rows 36 --layers 2 --t 256 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ROWS36 %s
// ROWS36: residual leaving layer 1: 36/36 rows bit-exact
// ROWS36: block 1's KV rows, all layers: 36/36 rows bit-exact
// ROWS36: block 1's 28 rows past the pass's: kept
// ROWS36: prefill of 2 layers, block 1, 36 rows: PASS
